From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu3d: a 48-bit GPU virtual address space (4 page table levels)

Direct3D feature level 12_2 wants at least 40 bits of GPU virtual address a
process; 3 levels of 512-entry page tables over 4 KB pages were 39. Four
levels give 48, as real GPUs have. The page tables stay what they were:
written by the CPU, read by nobody but Windows.
---
diff --git a/viogpu/common/helper.h b/viogpu/common/helper.h
index 22c678b..acb4d55 100644
--- a/viogpu/common/helper.h
+++ b/viogpu/common/helper.h
@@ -108,10 +108,10 @@ extern "C"
 #define VIOGPU_WDDM2 0
 #endif
 
-// GPU page tables (VIOGPU_WDDM2): 3 levels of 512 entries (DXGK_PTE, 16 bytes: 8 KB a table) over 4 KB pages, a
-// 39-bit (512 GB) GPU virtual address space. The CPU updates them (DXGK_PAGETABLEUPDATE_CPU_VIRTUAL) and the virtual
+// GPU page tables (VIOGPU_WDDM2): 4 levels of 512 entries (DXGK_PTE, 16 bytes: 8 KB a table) over 4 KB pages, a
+// 48-bit GPU virtual address space (Direct3D feature level 12_2 wants at least 40 bits a process). The CPU updates them (DXGK_PAGETABLEUPDATE_CPU_VIRTUAL) and the virtual
 // GPU never reads them: its commands name host resources, not addresses
-#define VIOGPU_PAGE_TABLE_LEVELS     3
+#define VIOGPU_PAGE_TABLE_LEVELS     4
 #define VIOGPU_PAGE_TABLE_INDEX_BITS 9
 #define VIOGPU_PAGE_TABLE_SIZE       ((1 << VIOGPU_PAGE_TABLE_INDEX_BITS) * 16)
 #define VIOGPU_GPU_VA_BITS           (VIOGPU_PAGE_TABLE_LEVELS * VIOGPU_PAGE_TABLE_INDEX_BITS + 12)
